Starting a series in Azure DevOps;

🚀 Day 1 — Azure Virtual Machines + Networking Fundamentals

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your application is running on Azure VMs and experiencing performance issues during peak hours. How will you design autoscaling using VM Scale Sets?

2️⃣ A VM deployed in a private subnet cannot access the internet for updates. How will you troubleshoot and fix this in Azure?

3️⃣ You need to expose an application securely running on Azure VMs to the internet. How will you design this using Azure Load Balancer or Application Gateway?

4️⃣ A production VM was accidentally deleted. How will you design backup and recovery to avoid data loss and reduce RTO/RPO?

5️⃣ You need to deploy identical VMs across environments (dev, test, prod). How will you standardize VM creation in Azure?

6️⃣ Your VM requires high availability across data centers. How will you architect this using Availability Sets vs Availability Zones?

7️⃣ An application requires static outbound IPs from Azure VMs. How will you configure networking to achieve this?

8️⃣ A VM is compromised due to open ports. How will you secure VM access using NSGs, Azure Bastion, and Just-In-Time access?

9️⃣ You must encrypt OS and data disks for compliance. How will you implement disk encryption and key management in Azure?

🔟 VM boot time is slow due to heavy configuration scripts. How will you optimize startup using custom images or cloud-init?

1️⃣1️⃣ You need to monitor CPU, memory, and disk performance of Azure VMs centrally. Which Azure monitoring services will you use?

1️⃣2️⃣ An application running on VMs needs to scale based on queue length rather than CPU. How will you design this scaling logic?

1️⃣3️⃣ You want to restrict VM creation only to approved regions and VM sizes. How will you enforce this at subscription level?

1️⃣4️⃣ A legacy VM-based application needs to be migrated from on-prem to Azure with minimal downtime. Which Azure services will you use?

1️⃣5️⃣ You must design a cost-optimized VM architecture for non-production workloads. What VM types and scheduling strategies will you use?

